# Cloudflare Pages routing for the hosted remote client (app.ananremote.com).
# Ships inside the bundle so every `wrangler pages deploy` of wwwroot carries
# it — this rule used to live only in the dashboard, and a deploy without it
# sent /go/<CALL> to the SPA fallback with no query (upstream QRZ wall).
# The client also parses /go/<CALL> from the path itself (remote-client.ts),
# so this rewrite is the canonical form, not a single point of failure.
/go/:call   /?remote=:call   302
# The operator manual is a static wwwroot asset (CI and the Pages flow both
# drop the built PDF in at deploy time), so the hosted client serves it
# directly. /manual stays alive for old bookmarks and pre-1.44 About links;
# radio-side, the /manual endpoint issues the same redirect.
/manual     /Zeus-Operator-Manual.pdf    302
